# SABOTAGE: A4 (ADR-047 §5.3; ADR-040 §4.4 / INV-1) gate sabotage — proposal provenance
# stops being token-only: `Samen.AI.Agent.WriteProposal`'s `proposal_reason/1` writes the
# tool kind and the VALIDATED ARG VALUES into the approval row's `reason` column. That is
# raw action input persisted in a governed row, in plaintext, OUTSIDE the DEK envelope —
# exactly what the engine's no-persisted-inputs rule exists to prevent, and the shape that
# would put a tenant identifier (or anything a permissive host tool accepts as an arg) into
# a row the vault's crypto-shred never reaches. The named token-only-provenance red (the
# approval row carries NO arg values) must flip, together with its physical-row twin,
# proving the property is asserted at both the Ash and the raw-column layer.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/ai/agent_write_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: the approval row carries NO arg values
# MUST_FAIL: the PHYSICAL approval row holds no arg value either
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent/write_proposal.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent/write_proposal.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent/write_proposal.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/ai/agent/write_proposal.ex
@@ -162,7 +162,12 @@
   # a gate is not a licence — a `reason` carrying arg values would be raw proposal input
   # persisted in a governed row, in plaintext, outside the DEK envelope. Sabotage 253 puts
   # them there and the named token-only-provenance test flips.
-  defp proposal_reason(_proposal), do: nil
+  # SABOTAGE (A4, ADR-040 §4.4 / INV-1): the proposal's raw inputs are persisted on the
+  # approval row's freeform `reason` column — outside the DEK envelope, unreachable by the
+  # run's crypto-shred, and visible to every approver surface.
+  defp proposal_reason(proposal) do
+    "#{Map.get(proposal, :tool_kind)} #{Jason.encode!(Map.get(proposal, :args, %{}))}"
+  end
 
   @doc """
   The bounded, TOKEN-ONLY provenance of a proposal, re-derived from governed domain state
